.TH smi-pki-intermediate-ca-extensions "1" "September 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI PKI Command"
.SH NAME
smi-pki-intermediate-ca-extensions \- Write Intermediate CA OpenSSL extensions to a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-pki-intermediate-ca-extensions
.I OUT_EXT_FILE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Writes the Intermediate CA extensions to \fIOUT_EXT_FILE\fR: basicConstraints=critical,CA:TRUE,pathlen:0, keyUsage=critical,keyCertSign,cRLSign, subjectKeyIdentifier=hash, authorityKeyIdentifier=keyid,issuer.
It is a thin command line wrapper over the matching function in the file based PKI library
\fBpki.sh\fR, so each step of building a CA and signing certificates can be run and inspected
on its own. All material is passed as file names; the command fails if the underlying OpenSSL
operation fails.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR smi-pki-ca-create (1),
.BR smi-pki-create-domain-cert (1),
.BR openssl (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Imre Tabur <imre.tabur@mail.ee>
